While playing yesterday, I received the following message on level 30-something.

"BURRPPP!!!
You have a sad feeling for a moment, then it passes..."

I knew that this meant one of my pets had died, but assumed it was the dog
I'd just tamed with some tripe because, of course, there's nothing on the
level that could kill my other pet - an Archon armed with Demonbane. Blow
the magic whistle - the dog appears. Put on a towel - wait. Where'd the  
Archon go? I searched the level and found the sword, but no corpse. I'm
assuming that this is because angels just don't leave corpses. My question,
then, is what killed him? The only monster in the area was a 'w' (long worm)
which I dispatched with a few blows. Not only does a long worm not seem
tough enough to kill an Archon, but what caused the BURRP message? I'd
guess it was because he got swallowed by something (Is that it?), but I've
never been swallowed by a long worm, only purple worms. Anyone care to guess
about what exactly happened here? My character's strong enough to survive
without the Archon, but I'm sort of taken aback by his death. There really
was nothing remotely powerful on the level - not even a minotaur, lich,
or the like, and even those shouldn't have given him much trouble.

